# language: en
@inventory @smoke
Feature: Cucumber inventory
  As a greengrocer
  I want to track how many cucumbers I have
  So that I never run out

  Background:
    Given the shop "Green & Co" is open
    And the stock is reset

  Scenario: Eat 5 out of 12
    Given there are 12 cucumbers
    When I eat 5 cucumbers
    Then I should have 7 cucumbers

  Scenario: Eat 5 out of 20
    Given there are 20 cucumbers
    When I eat 5 cucumbers
    Then I should have 15 cucumbers
    But I should not see the message 'Out of stock'

  @wip
  Scenario Outline: Eating cucumbers
    Given there are <start> cucumbers
    When I eat <eat> cucumbers
    Then I should have <left> cucumbers

    Examples: small amounts
      | start | eat | left |
      |    12 |   5 |    7 |
      |    20 |   5 |   15 |

    Examples: escaped cells
      | start | eat | left | note          |
      |     1 |   1 |    0 | a \| b        |

  Scenario: Restocking from a delivery note
    Given the following delivery note:
      """
      Supplier: "Farm \"Sunny\" Fields"
      Cucumbers: 40
      """
    When the note is processed
    Then the stock should be "40 \"fresh\" cucumbers"
    * the log contains 'restocked \'cucumbers\''

  Rule: Stock can never go negative

    Example: Eating more than we have
      Given there are 3 cucumbers
      When I eat 4 cucumbers
      Then I should see an error

# From https://gist.github.com/dogoku/0c024c55ec124355f01472abc70550f5
